<title>USA: U.S. cotton weekly export sales highlights--USDA.</title>
<headline>U.S. cotton weekly export sales highlights--USDA.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>USDA cotton export sales highlights in latest reporting week:</p>
<p>Net Upland sales of 153,300 running bales (RB) were four times the previous week and double the 4-week average.  The major increases were for Mexico (79,900 RB), Thailand (11,600 RB), China (11,000 RB), Indonesia (11,000 RB), and Japan (9,800 RB).</p>
<p>Exports of 176,000 RB--the fifth consecutive marketing-year high--exceeded the prior week by one-quarter and the 4-week average by 48 percent.  Asian destinations accounted for 66 percent of the week's shipments; Western Hemisphere, 23 percent; East European, 6 percent; and West European, 5 percent.</p>
</text>
